# Snyk authentication

## Cursor automations (weekly dependency scan)

Cloud agents **do not** receive GitHub Actions secrets. Configure **`SNYK_TOKEN`** (long-lived API token) as a **Runtime Secret** in [Cursor Cloud Agents → Secrets](https://cursor.com/dashboard/cloud-agents).

Run scans via `./scripts/run-snyk-scan.sh` (see `AGENTS.md`). Setup: `docs/security/snyk-automation-setup.md`.

## GitHub Actions CI

`.github/workflows/security-scans.yml` uses **`SNYK_TOKEN`** (preferred) with optional `SNYK_OAUTH_TOKEN` fallback.

Set GitHub secret:

```bash
./scripts/set-snyk-github-secret.sh YOUR_API_TOKEN
```

## OAuth (short-lived, ~1h)

`scripts/refresh-snyk-oauth-secret.ps1` syncs `snyk auth` → `SNYK_OAUTH_TOKEN` for ad-hoc CI only. **Not suitable for cron automations** — use API token instead.

## On any Snyk request

1. Prefer long-lived `SNYK_TOKEN` over OAuth for automation and CI.
2. Offer setup guide when auth fails: `docs/security/snyk-automation-setup.md`.
3. Keep Snyk in security-scans.yml alongside Trivy, Semgrep, Gitleaks, npm audit.
